  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "General term $=T_{r+1}$<br />$={ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_r\\left(\\frac{10}{x}\\right)^{10-r}\\left(\\frac{x}{10}\\right)^r$<br />Here $n=10$, which is an even number.<br />Now, $\\left[\\frac{10}{2}+1\\right]^{\\text {th }}$ term i.e. $6^{\\text {th }}$ term is the middle term.<br />Hence, middle term $=T_6$<br />$\\mathrm{T}_{5+1}={ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_5\\left(\\frac{10}{x}\\right)^{10-5}\\left(\\frac{x}{10}\\right)^5$<br />$={ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_5\\left(\\frac{10}{x}\\right)^5\\left(\\frac{x}{10}\\right)^5={ }^{10} \\mathrm{C}_5$.",
    "image": null
  },
